PRE-TABLE BLOCK -- #524 armbdt, TABLE 3 (the clause-(d) closure)
================================================================

WHY A THIRD TABLE.  Table 2 measured M_MASK1 -- the fix present, its mask
weakened 0xfffffffc -> 0xfffffffe -- at 25/25.  A MEASURED TOTAL ESCAPE, and
a clause-(d) floor breach: the fix IS the mask, so a weakened mask is the
canonical (d) form (the carrier's own #461 `m_align1' shape, & 3 -> & 1).

THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE, NOT AN APPEND TO PRETABLE.out.  The ledger records
an appended section destroying a PRETABLE's mtime once, and the mtime is the
whole evidentiary value of this artifact -- it is what proves the block was
written BEFORE the answers were known.

ROWS ADDED, AND THE MUTANT EACH KILLS
-------------------------------------
  ARM_LDM_COLD_DATA_P2   kills M_MASK1.  Channel: r1 after ldmia from base
                         0x20002.  Correct (& ~3) masks to 0x20000 -> r1 =
                         0x11223344.  Mutant (& ~1) leaves 0x20002 -> reads
                         bytes[2..5] = 22 11 88 77 -> r1 = 0x77881122.
                         THE CHANNEL VARIES UNDER THE NAMED MUTANT.

  ARM_STM_COLD_DATA_P2   kills M_MASK1.  Channel: the word at PAGE_STM after
                         stmia to base 0x21002.  Correct -> 0x11223344.
                         Mutant stores at 0x21002, straddling, so PAGE_STM
                         reads 0x33440000.

  ARM_LDM_PATH_COLD_P2   PATH control for the row above -- establishes the
  ARM_STM_PATH_COLD_P2   +2 runs actually took the COLD path.  Without it a
                         green DATA row cannot say WHICH path produced it,
                         which is the whole symptom of this defect.

WHY +3 IS NOT ROWED
-------------------
  ~1 dies at +2 (above).  ~2 already dies at +1 (the existing rows).  So a +3
  row kills no ENUMERATED mutant.  Rows are owed PER ENUMERATED MUTANT, never
  per reachable value -- rowing +3 would be the unbounded-growth shape the
  row-demand bound exists to refuse.  RESIDUE 3 IS DISCLOSED IN THE CONTRACT.

PREDICTIONS -- WRITTEN BEFORE THE RUN, AND PREDICTIONS ONLY
-----------------------------------------------------------
  BASE           30/30   (the fix; all rows green)
  HEAD           ?/30    RED on the cold DATA rows incl. both new ones
  M_MASK1        ?/30    MUST GO RED on ARM_LDM_COLD_DATA_P2 and
                         ARM_STM_COLD_DATA_P2.  If it does not, the closure
                         has failed and the round does not ship.
  M_ENTRY        ?/30    RED on the writeback rows, as before
  M_NULL_MEDIUM  ?/30    RED on everything that observes a transfer

  *** THESE ARE PREDICTIONS.  The measured values go in SCORES.txt and any
  record citing a number cites THAT file, never this one.  Table 1's
  PRETABLE predicted M_NULL_MEDIUM 4/25 and the measurement was 6/25 -- the
  prediction rested on a wrong claim that every row observes block transfer,
  when ARM_STM_COLD_CLOBBER and THUMB_PUSH_COLD_CLOBBER are identity rows
  under a medium that writes nothing.  A prediction in a measured column is
  the frozen-number class; this block keeps them in separate sections. ***
